**THIS GRANT AGREEMENT** is made on 15 July 2025 by and between:

(1) **MERIDIAN COMMUNITY TRUST**, a charity registered in Singapore under the Charities Act (Cap. 37) with Unique Entity Number S72SS0011H and having its registered office at 12 Raffles Quay, #18-01 Hong Leong Building, Singapore 048545 (the **"Trust"**); and

(2) **LAKESIDE FAMILY SERVICES**, a company limited by guarantee incorporated in Singapore with Unique Entity Number 198802345C and having its registered office at 20 Jurong Gateway Road, #09-01, Singapore 608451 (the **"Recipient"**).

The Trust and the Recipient are each referred to as a **"Party"** and together as the **"Parties"**.

---

**RECITALS**

**WHEREAS:**

(A) The Trust is a philanthropic organisation established to support community-based programmes that address social needs and empower vulnerable groups in Singapore.

(B) The Recipient is a social service agency that has been operating in the Jurong area for over 35 years, providing family support services, youth development programmes, and community outreach initiatives.

(C) The Recipient has submitted a grant proposal dated 10 March 2025 to the Trust seeking funding for the Youth Empowerment Project (the **"Programme"**), a three-year initiative designed to support at-risk youth aged 13 to 18 in the Jurong and Boon Lay constituencies.

(D) The Trust has approved the grant application and wishes to provide funding to the Recipient for the implementation of the Programme, subject to the terms and conditions set out in this Agreement.

**NOW IT IS HEREBY AGREED** as follows:

---

**1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION**

1.1 In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:

The Youth Empowerment Project grant_amount is 250000 SGD. Record status: current.

**"Agreement"** means this Grant Agreement, including all Schedules and any amendments made in accordance with Clause 13;

**"Business Day"** means a day (other than a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday) on which banks are open for general business in Singapore;

**"Commencement Date"** means 1 August 2025;

**"Completion Date"** means 31 July 2028;

**"Confidential Information"** has the meaning set out in Clause 9.1;

**"Control"** means the ability, whether direct or indirect, to direct the affairs of another person, whether by virtue of shareholding, contract, or otherwise;

**"Designated Account"** means the bank account designated by the Recipient for receipt of the Grant, details of which are set out in Schedule 1;

**"Effective Date"** means the date of this Agreement as stated in the opening paragraph;

**"Financial Year"** means the financial year of the Recipient, commencing 1 April and ending 31 March;

**"Grant"** means the grant amount specified in Clause 2.1;

**"Grant Period"** means the period from the Commencement Date to the Completion Date;

**"Laws"** means all applicable laws, regulations, codes, guidelines, and directives in Singapore, including but not limited to the Charities Act (Cap. 37), the Companies Act (Cap. 50), and the Code of Governance for Charities and IPCs;

**"Programme"** means the Youth Empowerment Project as described in Schedule 1;

**"Programme Outcomes"** means the outcomes and performance indicators set out in Schedule 2;

**"Reporting Schedule"** means the schedule of reports required to be submitted by the Recipient to the Trust, as set out in Schedule 2;

**"S$" and "SGD"** mean Singapore Dollars, the lawful currency of Singapore.
